+  FAILED round 1 of `chore/gate0-truth-and-dbt-deadwood` for exactly its absence and was right —
+  the same finding as 2026-07-31 and 2026-08-01 above: "Recording a ruling in the contract is not
+  recording it." Three rulings on the same rule now; the rule holds.
+
+  WHAT WAS APPROVED. GitLab issue #33 is the working brief for the pipeline stream, produced by
+  three independent expert assessments (warehouse modelling, ingestion/raw, orchestration) plus a
+  synthesis that adjudicated the conflicts between them. On 2026-08-08 the CPO said "yes" to all
+  three headline decisions and then approved the full recommendation set. Verbatim, as given to the
+  builder:
+
+    "Every item in #33's Gate 0, Wave 1, Wave 2 and Wave 3 is APPROVED, including the two that
+    would normally be CPO-class: raw merge-on-write with the raw_archive backup first (item 8),
+    and staging materialised as a table (item 9). The CPO said 'yes' to all three headline
+    decisions on 2026-08-08 and then approved the full recommendation set."
+
+  The same instruction supplies the §1 Confirm for every task in the stream ("Work through the plan
+  without checking in on anything #33 already settles") and directs that this paragraph be quoted
+  as the authority in each contract's `protected_override` or `decisions_taken`, citing #33.
+
+  THE §10-CLASS ITEMS THIS COVERS, named individually so a later reader does not have to infer the
+  scope of "the full recommendation set":
+  - Item 7 — CREATE THE GITLAB NIGHTLY SCHEDULE, 04:00 UTC, branch main, activated. A recurring
+    cost, therefore CPO-class. Not a NEW recurring cost: `.github/workflows/dbt-scheduled.yml` ran
+    the same job on the same cron until 2026-08-06 and the migration dropped it silently.
+  - Item 8 — RAW MERGE-ON-WRITE on the eight append-only raw tables, keyed on `league_code`.
+    Permanently discards ingest history beyond BigQuery's 7-day time travel, hence CPO-class. The
+    approval is CONDITIONAL ON THE BACKUP: a one-off copy of each raw table into a `raw_archive`
+    dataset FIRST (~$0.30/mo on ~15 GiB), which is what makes it reversible.
+  - Item 9 — STAGING MATERIALISED AS A TABLE (`1_staging: +materialized: table`). A storage-cost
